[{"id":"VRCE-6-40-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":1,"english":"Then out spoke the highly energetic and exceedingly mighty king of monkeys, “Why is this host agitated like a bark driven hither and thither by the wind?\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e14a1613cc3b0ac3d17fe3cd5d08a6810d3ef1704c1851c2bad96a9fc503ece1","compact":"76dfb422158d346e2c17f64c7c02fa5ab0c2796ea45259a8d4425a422745cf57","nasal":"76dfb422158d346e2c17f64c7c02fa5ab0c2796ea45259a8d4425a422745cf57"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":2,"english":"Hearing Sugriva's speech, Vali's son said, Did you not see both those heroes-sons of Dasaratha, Rama and that mighty car-warriorLakşmaņa-covered with arrows?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.941,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5f2899e46c9eb2664bf1141383e932fcab3a3c45855293500469913846422466","compact":"77f3b88502166aadbe7cc31af4679b3cc10d9df28a307b7fd0354ffd9acb5013","nasal":"a3eb0e37f2fe6a2e17e2249993dcc87c203bf58f1cd88c023f843d8bc58680e2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":3,"english":"And (did you not see) those high-should ones lying in the field of battle, covered with blood ?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6cb59c9c72047969d14ebad5a6921fe3da53100d3350c8e445d0001b75aaa980","compact":"1b3d2e12a10a871d01dcb2a3d9445bd68af7e36b2f6f78861c4b861c51ba2001","nasal":"1b3d2e12a10a871d01dcb2a3d9445bd68af7e36b2f6f78861c4b861c51ba2001"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":4,"english":"Thereat, the lord of monkeys, Sugrīva, spoke to his son, Angada \"I do not deem it without cause. This may have come to pass through sheer fear.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bb3cec055985d304ee4e577e666bb7dfb9621ea42efa5281241ad2bc8bb166dc","compact":"68e7b6a563d704632df648f4bd3237a840382f8a3b4c1ff8bfc4f2b85cae29fd","nasal":"6f9276c77ad21c2410bbec2dba502eeee748ff603a9b118889fcb5f46a912899"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":5,"english":"These monkeys with sad faces, leaving their arms behind them are flying in all directions, their eyes distended in affright.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.73,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d27bc1d4f08b94281ce74789912bebd37a7f54c9473454b40203986becc70a88","compact":"4d73663d19a61e8497588aeba61e3e4cd1cbdcf56f662cba28744d7d39f71510","nasal":"955a5154b1783f7d450e0123a5ea7784ee42000c6c3c1dc6c598d85bb4539297"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":6,"english":"They are not ashamed of each other, and they do not cast their looks back. And they hug each other, and go leaping over the fallen.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c3a8