unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"51e42f914f9701f2ee153ec60b69ceaa128b293ed5aec9be31fe6eaee627bf76","compact":"e269924df706169652629e39b079d13a5f537335a5ab0782a14d4deab25d08e4","nasal":"a7deca89b61209eea3b33bc9f46daac2b7dd2344a7d54d1aadbb255ec5604916"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":10,"english":"Do you at once stay these agitated with fear and scampering all around; and proclaim, 'This is Vibhisana, who has come here.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.87,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c338e8b0b7e8c122a90b8a4cfa8da25bdd7cdfe9f3144fce0c4dbeaa3f6471dd","compact":"861a165e1565a546e587805f43a0b4f68a350b5b018ac7fc3aa2c2f52f280750","nasal":"861a165e1565a546e587805f43a0b4f68a350b5b018ac7fc3aa2c2f52f280750"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":11,"english":"Thus directed, Jõmbavān-king of bearsrestraining those that were flying, composed the monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.929,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b344ea35f64fed40f898da4b9f347f6e5e72db50ff8b21459964434e327a025d","compact":"2ca07adb198a1ee05348177a14688a077b8e7ffb358e16bacb1526fa1da6c16f","nasal":"6c2027dc3e9a012bacab1681cd2d611320b0a0b1628a42a9dc03ddf67a11de2c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":12,"english":"Hearing the bear-king's words, and seeing Vibhisana, the monkeys, renouncing fear, desisted (from their flight).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"405e20d04ae63f6628ab77a8fa196c223b6a00fde95da5ea37463a3bb52fbe7c","compact":"c202242604fdf2515cf3199414e533c8057fe2d64026bf7cc350840ff06943ac","nasal":"c202242604fdf2515cf3199414e533c8057fe2d64026bf7cc350840ff06943ac"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":13,"english":"Then the righteous Vibhīșaņa, viewing Rama's as well as Laksmana's body pierced with arrows, was exceedingly aggrieved.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.764,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"42ac47f7e493495ec5bcf7681989ec7f594a2fce0e1637a4bcbb4009944db98b","compact":"e8c526960612b0929e517cb604348b2a2a3f15ef7c61eda5dab42010e2d1dfbc","nasal":"90bba1ed87659ccbdaa9b51091b46d3955e80f9ff6034f8bd15241d3bc6fd474"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":14,"english":"Washing their eyes with water, he, with his mind overpowered with grief, began to weep and broke out into lamentation.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.745,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4e1f9bd51d0fcdefff10a075b2fb0c4623c9483bca8baab4e0fb23f56b0598f8","compact":"14cf5f9eb0a9c5df1460bdb64905eff659105d313f86de75edffbc8e088548a6","nasal":"66042ac838ea085687b84bd427b1c55ad278e2f8fff72befb1a630846086b783"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":15,"english":"The Rāksasas, fighting in wily ways, have brought to this pass these ones endowed with prowess and possessed of every perfection and gifted with might (of arm).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.889,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"065ef46f562ef02f622088508b04820ca29db1c205fed3ca7d22757b003fcd53","compact":"7b4446e2f5a884bae40515d978337987ddaf559fe91b4baa2d9278558eb43ef6","nasal":"6d12fea17c8238300f5f1030951396b3962fc4e86349aff6a4bf3739ec989f93"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":16,"english":"And with his guileful mind, that brother's son of mine, wicked-souled and an evil son (to me), has deceived these ones of straight prowess.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.653,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4f9b42fcea4c96f62033ae3d1d7a1e3448aea74f79e57bc6e04363ff136b4936","compact":"218d23fbc1fb809a7e5a0b7016784298bd0a209f09a915986f0b7da81e9a3588","nasal":"218d23fbc1fb809a7e5a0b7016784298bd0a209f09a915986f0b7da81e9a3588"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":17,"english":"Pierced with innumerable shafts, and covered with blood, these are lying on the ground like Salyakas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3f94c0f67a6ef55c8f3836fa20c0c2f208d3183a0aadb80379dcc84e36bcbb1b","compact":"3b37e31ab22b4aa75c8b746cf7152f5ece589ad0feb7f1b36eb73db6474a2388","nasal":"3b37e31ab22b4aa75c8b746cf7152f5ece589ad0feb7f1b36eb73db6474a2388"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":18,"english":"Those depending on whose prowess, I had sought eminence, those foremost of men, sleep here soundly for renouncing their bodies.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.739,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0eafee2cf9b1a722df10300ada46754200ded09b6bee835806390373924d0e24","compact":"93f801f0455b7b833626cdb89d2e85f18933ba26f77920f97c3828c4419a5b0a","nasal":"2f293f7a03cd95089b6ba51ff06bf58d0011a25aa9f40873bdd13857d1660225"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":19,"english":"Living, today I am in distress: and my desire of dominion is annihilated; and my foe, Rāvana, has his promise fulfilled and his aim crowned with success.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c8030c73cbfb724bd6cd1a1d93b6c5bd45a11a1716f44c36b4a4b7a13390e537","compact":"9ac497722effa41b8a86dcb60410fdc1d30267aabbe5a7120ea5efc629f6e3c0","nasal":"5fdc348876d57b1df8fa065c44b7d85997d2cc9bcbd4885faf5ff060a0dbca14"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":20,"english":"As Vibhīşana was thus lamenting, the lord of monkeys-Sugriva-endowed with strength, embracing him spoke to him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ce152a582cdc1f17c2199b9207ba454e606c8e0cf29724be826d42ba326ee490","compact":"6fbe1874b74716c18e91d40c56a4c8d861f7296a1e4fb583056c8be3a3fb36d4","nasal":"7c69c6ab31740c20bed4b503bed8cb724d4c7aa50f7e11b636b78df8ef625415"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":21,"english":"O you cognisant of righteousness, you will here in Lankā obtain empire: no doubt of this; and Răvaņa along with his sons will be disappointed in their expectations.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.657,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3a3f79b611b7c7fe641cc5a3b0d23239db40bc271e897349afdf2eaffa01fe48","compact":"738abb401008f98bfd703922afa2dbee4078255b34f8125b3a75d3384172b22c","nasal":"0379f9281f88790f8f1d8b28edba85afc61dec4571b090df1f4bae958e727985"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":22,"english":"Both these-Rāma and Lakşmaņa-are under the aegis of Garuda; and, casting off their stupor: they will in battle slay Rävaņa along with his adherents.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040022","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"edf9ddc1ff7c36f49d3bef248a598b565788492c05ca78fcb8bac4bf16b8701c","compact":"38fa4f9de02c950832ef47a6045fce9ae1c66e7bcba81b5286457854d8512df7","nasal":"38fa4f9de02c950832ef47a6045fce9ae1c66e7bcba81b5286457854d8512df7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-40-23","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":40,"verse":23,"english":"Having thus soothed and comforted the Raksasa, Sugriva addressed his father-in-law, who was at his side, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.706,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-50-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6040023","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9c6efaf3127fd8c5f648c10a601e3c420dac3916d10f4b8cfbaecf26b4e2d